# Step 1a prerequisite drift review

Run: physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14
Role: alpha
Scope: the 62 A pages in the run ledger

This is a page-prerequisite review, not proof acceptance. I compared the canonical plan and each assigned manifest with the current QFT, relativistic-particle-mechanics, and thermodynamics research designs. The local arguments and source maps remain research evidence; they do not certify future item proofs.

Existing published mathematical pages with exact current supplier mappings were added as backward prerequisites. The NRQM page edge for TD8 follows the audited consumer mapping. No item, page content, manifest, scope ledger, import, or engine state was edited.

## Owner holds

E1 — The planned MP2 page td-math-nonsmooth-equilibrium uses the published item thm-hessian-characterises-convexity in its M2 Hessian criterion. Its home page, convex-and-semicontinuous-functions-on-rn, exists in the mathematical library but is absent from this plan and therefore has no plan order. The current proof design uses it for the constrained-curvature/stability claims, including the later TD4 stability claim. The owner must add the published page as prerequisite context or authorize a complete local proof of that criterion. This hold propagates through MP2's declared consumers.

E2 — MP6's L16 and L17 arguments use the published Brownian construction, Ito-isometry/deterministic-Gaussian-integral, and Birkhoff suppliers. Their home pages brownian-motion-construction-and-continuity, the-ito-integral-with-respect-to-brownian-motion, and the-ergodic-theorems-of-von-neumann-and-birkhoff are absent from the canonical plan and have no plan orders. The consuming claims are thm-tdmath-ornstein-uhlenbeck-model and the finite-measure Hamiltonian recurrence/ergodic results. The owner must authorize those existing pages as prerequisite context or require complete local suppliers.

E3 — MP8's L21/L22 proofs use Kolmogorov extension, uniformly-integrable martingale convergence, von Neumann mean convergence, and convergence-in-probability-to-L1 suppliers. Their home pages infinite-product-measures-and-kolmogorov-extension, martingale-inequalities-and-convergence, the-ergodic-theorems-of-von-neumann-and-birkhoff, and modes-of-convergence-for-random-variables are absent from the canonical plan and have no plan orders. The consuming claims are thm-tdmath-local-tame-entropy-compactness and thm-tdmath-spatial-mean-information; MP9 and TD12 consume those results downstream. The owner must authorize the existing pages as prerequisite context or require complete local suppliers.

No order was invented for an absent plan page. The engine must hold these affected pages for owner resolution.

